    "summary": "The push wears off within a week, and it costs push permission for good.",
    "explanation": "The overall +4.5% (p < 0.001) is the average of a first week where the push felt new and a second week where it barely matters. Meanwhile push opt-outs rose 45.9%, and opt-outs do not come back when the novelty fades. The trade is a temporary bump in posting for the permanent loss of a channel.",
    "issueNotes": {
      "novelty": "The lift in posting was +8.9% in the first week but only +0.1% in the last (p = 0.966): the push stopped working as people got used to it.",
      "guardrail": "Push opt-outs rose 45.9% (p < 0.001). Every user who turns off push is a user you can no longer reach, for this feature or any other."
    },
    "recommendation": "Kill the daily push. To nudge posting, test a rarer, more personal trigger (a close friend posting for the first time in a while) and judge it on its last week and on opt-outs.",
